          'The if-clause can come first or second. Use a comma only when the if-clause comes first (Life would be very boring if we couldn\'t contact our friends).',
          'With the verb "be" we usually use "were" for all persons: If I were you, I would take a break.',
          'Negative: wouldn\'t (would not) / couldn\'t. Question: What would you do if you were him?',
          'Could or might can replace would to show ability or possibility: If I had time, I could help you.',
